        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-5">
  <h2 class="mb-4">About the Project</h2>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-8">
      <p>The PDSA-II Game Project is an interactive exploration of classic algorithm problems implemented as games. Each game demonstrates different algorithm approaches, with performance metrics to compare efficiency.</p>
      <p>This project was developed as part of the PDSA-II coursework to demonstrate practical applications of data structures and algorithms.</p>
      <h4 class="mt-4">Featured Algorithms:</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Minimax and Monte Carlo Tree Search</strong> for game playing</li>
        <li><strong>Dynamic Programming, Greedy, and Genetic Algorithms</strong> for optimization</li>
        <li><strong>Backtracking and Heuristic approaches</strong> for constraint satisfaction</li>
        <li><strong>Recursive and Iterative implementations</strong> for classic problems</li>
        <li><strong>Sequential and Threaded approaches</strong> for performance comparison</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
